# PrivateFleet Overview

Mobile-first PWA for a private truck fleet: loads + trailer/tractor damage photos, Safety review/inbox, Admin users/roles.

Canonical plan: `docs/BUILD_PLAN.md`.

## Roles (MVP)

- **Driver** — unique `driver_id` at signup; log loads; upload trailer & tractor damage; send own images to Safety inbox.
- **Safety** — view-only fleet trailer/tractor damage; mark **viewed** (maps to `damage_notices` / noticed); Safety inbox of driver referrals.
- **Admin** — manage users/roles; full visibility; loads oversight. No exotic admin tooling.

## Stack

- **Next.js 16** App Router (`src/app`), React 19, React Compiler on
- **Tailwind CSS v4** (`@import "tailwindcss"` in `globals.css`)
- **Supabase Cloud**: Auth + Postgres + RLS — `@supabase/ssr` + `@supabase/supabase-js`
- **Cloudflare R2** for damage photos (S3 SDK); metadata in Postgres
- **Serwist** PWA (`@serwist/turbopack`)

## Source layout

- `src/app/(auth)/` — login, signup
- `src/app/(app)/` — dashboard, damage/*, tractor/*, safety/inbox, admin/users, export (bottom nav shell; role-aware)
- `src/app/api/` — route handlers (`health`, `uploads/presign`)
- `src/lib/supabase/` — browser, server, middleware clients
- `src/lib/r2.ts`, `src/lib/canvas-export.ts`
- `src/components/{auth,camera,damage,export,loads,pwa,safety,admin}/`
- `src/types/database.ts` — hand-typed row shapes until `supabase gen types`
- `supabase/migrations/` — schema source of truth

## Path alias

Use `@/*` → `src/*` (see `tsconfig.json`).

## Product rules

- Signup must pass `driver_id` in auth user metadata for drivers (profile trigger reads it).
- Planned: `profiles.role` (`driver` | `safety` | `admin`); tractor via `asset_type` (or equivalent); Safety inbox/referrals table.
- Damage photos → R2; DB stores `r2_key` / optional `r2_url` + GPS + timestamp + asset/driver snapshots.
- **Viewed** = new notice/view row (`damage_notices` today), never duplicate photos. Drivers send-to-Safety ≠ viewed.
- Canvas export: photo + white metadata strip → composite JPG.
- Prefer mobile (`max-w-lg`), touch-friendly UI; keep bottom nav in `(app)/layout`.

## Do not

- Commit `.env.local` or put secrets in rules/docs.
- Invent schema columns — extend via new migrations + update `src/types/database.ts`.
- Bypass RLS with the service role from the browser.
